---
Description: "Go DDD Architecture Guidelines"
Globs:
  - "**/*.go"
---

# Directory Structure
- cmd/bot/main.go for the application entry point
- internal/domain/ for domain models (entities, value objects, domain interfaces)
- app/ for application services (orchestrating domain logic)
- infrastructure/ for external implementations (database, external APIs)
- config/ for configuration
- pkg/ for shared libraries
- tests/ for integration or end-to-end tests

# Domain Layer
- Keep domain logic pure. No direct references to external packages or frameworks.
- Define repository interfaces here. Implement them in infrastructure.

# Application Layer
- Orchestrates domain logic, transactions, and calls domain services.
- Thin layer: any heavy logic belongs in domain or domain services.

# Infrastructure Layer
- Database, external APIs, frameworks. 
- Must implement domain interfaces, not the other way around.

# Conventions
- Use Go modules. 
- Package naming: short, lowercase, no underscores.
- Error handling: prefer idiomatic Go errors, domain-specific errors in domain/errors.go.
- Testing: table-driven tests, store integration tests in /tests or co-located.
